{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013gGpSAncDKvKD91GsrNaRp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Portfolio Program â€” Sequence (the uber plan: cycles, not one build)\n2\t\n3\t> This is the program-level \"uber plan.\" It sequences the whole effort as a substrate build followed by a\n4\t> series of **per-skill cycles**, each of which is its OWN researchPrime deep-dive â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman\n5\t> â†’ Learn. The per-skill METHOD (what makes the skill best-in-class) is produced inside each cycle's research +\n6\t> Crucible â€” NOT in this document and NOT in the Phase-0 infra plan. This restores the original cadence:\n7\t> \"multiple waves of researchPrime deep-dives + crucible specific for each wave, with a foreman follow on.\"\n8\t\n9\t## Why cycles, not one monolithic build\n10\tA structural done-floor (â‰¥3 non-goals, â‰¥K canaries, gates green) produces a GENERIC skill. What makes Gandalf\n11\ta genuinely useful critical-review tool â€” or Ramanujan a genuinely useful math-understanding tool â€” is its\n12\tMETHOD: the best-in-class techniques it embodies. That method must be researched and forged per skill, before\n13\tits protocol and canaries can be written (you cannot author good Gandalf canaries before you know what expert\n14\tcritical review actually does). Hence: one cycle per skill.\n15\t\n16\t## The per-skill cycle TEMPLATE (every skill runs this)\n17\t1. **researchPrime deep-dive** (stakes-scaled, evidence-laddered) on: \"best-in-class METHOD for <skill domain> â€”\n18\t   named frameworks/techniques/reference practitioners; failure modes; what separates expert from novice; how\n19\t   to encode it as a stateless SKILL.md protocol.\" Output â†’ the skill's research deliverable.\n20\t2. **Skill Crucible** (Stage 0â†’1â†’2, Shark-vetted): forge the skill's locked NORTH-STAR (purpose + machine-\n21\t   checkable non-goals + invariants), the SKILL.md PROTOCOL (the method), the persona/model-tier, the canary\n22\t   set (core + discriminating negative canaries, FIX-17â€²), and the journal/improvement protocol. Emits a\n23\t   Foreman-ready handoff for the skill, gated by Phase-0 infra.\n24\t3. **Foreman build**: build the skill to the per-skill done-floor (Master Plan), using the Phase-0 eval harness,\n25\t   templates, journal schema, and handoff contract.\n26\t4. **Review / Learn**: Gandalf-style critical review (once Gandalf exists; bootstrap with the cross-family\n27\t   advisory judge + human for Gandalf itself) + run on 2â€“3 real tasks + seed the journal from genuine runs.\n28\t\n29\t## Sequence (dependency-ordered)\n30\t\n31\t### Stage A â€” Phase-0 shared infrastructure  [Foreman-ready NOW]\n32\t`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (6 waves). Build first; everything below depends on it.\n33\t\n34\t### Stage B â€” Cognitive-skill cycles (each = the template above)\n35\tOrdered so the recreate-a-paper proof's data flow is satisfied (understand â†’ lineage â†’ data â†’ code â†’ verify):\n36\t\n37\t1. **Gandalf â€” critical review.** First, because it is also the Review-stage engine for later cycles.\n38\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class critical analysis / red-teaming / analytic rigor â€” e.g. structured\n39\t     analytic techniques (Heuer, ACH), argument mapping, steelmanning, premortem, the discipline of \"what\n40\t     is actually going on here\"; failure modes (confirmation bias, motivated reasoning, sycophancy); how\n41\t     top-tier review differs from surface critique. Persona tier = Fable 5.\n42\t   - *Bootstrap note (A4):* Gandalf is gated by Phase-0 infra + a CROSS-FAMILY advisory judge + human review â€”\n43\t     NOT by itself.\n44\t2. **Ramanujan â€” math/algorithm understanding.** Emits the understandâ†’build firewall (pure, offline,\n45\t   deterministic reference fn + spec + unit tests) the proof depends on (FIX-8/18).\n46\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class mathematical exposition + algorithm comprehension â€” derivation-checking,\n47\t     worked-example pedagogy, the Feynman technique, proof verification, dimensional/sanity analysis; how to\n48\t     turn a paper's method prose into a verified, runnable reference. Persona tier = Fable 5 / Opus.\n49\t3. **Literature review** (augmented researchPrime). Upstream lineage/lit-review is load-bearing for paper-repro.\n50\t   - *Research framing:* systematic-review method, citation-lineage mining, recovering tacit knowledge from\n51\t     cited code; what a rigorous lit/lineage report contains. Persona tier = Opus.\n52\t4. **Data analysis** â€” find/clean/analyze/report.\n53\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class EDA, data cleaning/validation, result-comparison + plotting practice;\n54\t     reproducible data pipelines. Persona tier = Sonnetâ†’Opus.\n55\t5. **Analytic + ML code** â€” R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch.\n56\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class scientific/ML coding practice; satisfying a frozen firewall spec;\n57\t     dependency-aware modular generation. Persona tier = Opus.\n58\t6. **Code verification** (co-designed with #5).\n59\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class code-fidelity verification â€” visual artifacts a human can review,\n60\t     chunked walkthroughs, executed-number checks bound to a verified module (FIX-8). Persona = Fable 5.\n61\t\n62\t### Stage C â€” recreate-a-paper proof cycle  [needs Stage B skills]\n63\tIts own researchPrime (paper-repro pipeline SOTA â€” already partly done in Phase-0 research) + Crucible +\n64\tForeman. Composes the Stage-B skills; required upstream lineage/lit-review; Assumptions Ledger; understandâ†’build\n65\tfirewall; executed numbers BOUND to Ramanujan's pure reference fn; context-isolated advisory grader. The PROOF:\n66\treproduce Gelman ANOVA, graded on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (NOT fidelity).\n67\t\n68\t### Stage D â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration\n69\tInject a known defect (a seeded deterministic-canary regression) into a built skill; a real sleep cycle must\n70\tRECOVER it (regression-then-recovery) â€” a no-op cannot pass. The self-improving proof.\n71\t\n72\t### Later portfolio (own cycles, beyond this program's proof)\n73\tJumper (brainstorm), doc-writing, legal analysis, propose-extensions recipe, then the productivity/personal\n74\tstateful agents (model-agnostic; GWL/t2rs swap-in deferred â€” parallel track).\n75\t\n76\t## What stays fixed across all cycles (the substrate contract)\n77\tPhase-0 infra (Stage A) + the Master Plan design pillars + the per-skill done-floor + PRINCIPLE-D (deterministic\n78\tgate; advisory judging isolated) + the machine-checkable handoff contract. Each skill cycle inherits these; the\n79\tresearch + Crucible add the per-skill METHOD on top.\n80\t\n81\t## Open question to revisit (separate from this sequence)\n82\tAudit whether the TRIO skill PROTOCOLS (researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman SKILL.md method, not the engines)\n83\tare themselves best-in-class â€” a small researchPrime \"is this protocol SOTA for its domain?\" pass over each.\n84\tThe engines are demonstrably robust (the adversarial loops caught real flaws this program, including a wrong\n85\tfix); the method-depth of the protocols is the open question.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"724016eb-62f7-4d81-9999-a8b5811805f4","uuid":"e5b37022-201f-4dd2-a2ee-2afc59d4345b","timestamp":"2026-06-21T00:14:14.730Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/Skill Foundry/planning/portfolio-program/crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md","content":"# Portfolio Program â€” Sequence (the uber plan: cycles, not one build)\n\n> This is the program-level \"uber plan.\" It sequences the whole effort as a substrate build followed by a\n> series of **per-skill cycles**, each of which is its OWN researchPrime deep-dive â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman\n> â†’ Learn. The per-skill METHOD (what makes the skill best-in-class) is produced inside each cycle's research +\n> Crucible â€” NOT in this document and NOT in the Phase-0 infra plan. This restores the original cadence:\n> \"multiple waves of researchPrime deep-dives + crucible specific for each wave, with a foreman follow on.\"\n\n## Why cycles, not one monolithic build\nA structural done-floor (â‰¥3 non-goals, â‰¥K canaries, gates green) produces a GENERIC skill. What makes Gandalf\na genuinely useful critical-review tool â€” or Ramanujan a genuinely useful math-understanding tool â€” is its\nMETHOD: the best-in-class techniques it embodies. That method must be researched and forged per skill, before\nits protocol and canaries can be written (you cannot author good Gandalf canaries before you know what expert\ncritical review actually does). Hence: one cycle per skill.\n\n## The per-skill cycle TEMPLATE (every skill runs this)\n1. **researchPrime deep-dive** (stakes-scaled, evidence-laddered) on: \"best-in-class METHOD for <skill domain> â€”\n   named frameworks/techniques/reference practitioners; failure modes; what separates expert from novice; how\n   to encode it as a stateless SKILL.md protocol.\" Output â†’ the skill's research deliverable.\n2. **Skill Crucible** (Stage 0â†’1â†’2, Shark-vetted): forge the skill's locked NORTH-STAR (purpose + machine-\n   checkable non-goals + invariants), the SKILL.md PROTOCOL (the method), the persona/model-tier, the canary\n   set (core + discriminating negative canaries, FIX-17â€²), and the journal/improvement protocol. Emits a\n   Foreman-ready handoff for the skill, gated by Phase-0 infra.\n3. **Foreman build**: build the skill to the per-skill done-floor (Master Plan), using the Phase-0 eval harness,\n   templates, journal schema, and handoff contract.\n4. **Review / Learn**: Gandalf-style critical review (once Gandalf exists; bootstrap with the cross-family\n   advisory judge + human for Gandalf itself) + run on 2â€“3 real tasks + seed the journal from genuine runs.\n\n## Sequence (dependency-ordered)\n\n### Stage A â€” Phase-0 shared infrastructure  [Foreman-ready NOW]\n`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (6 waves). Build first; everything below depends on it.\n\n### Stage B â€” Cognitive-skill cycles (each = the template above)\nOrdered so the recreate-a-paper proof's data flow is satisfied (understand â†’ lineage â†’ data â†’ code â†’ verify):\n\n1. **Gandalf â€” critical review.** First, because it is also the Review-stage engine for later cycles.\n   - *Research framing:* best-in-class critical analysis / red-teaming / analytic rigor â€” e.g. structured\n     analytic techniques (Heuer, ACH), argument mapping, steelmanning, premortem, the discipline of \"what\n     is actually going on here\"; failure modes (confirmation bias, motivated reasoning, sycophancy); how\n     top-tier review differs from surface critique. Persona tier = Fable 5.\n   - *Bootstrap note (A4):* Gandalf is gated by Phase-0 infra + a CROSS-FAMILY advisory judge + human review â€”\n     NOT by itself.\n2. **Ramanujan â€” math/algorithm understanding.** Emits the understandâ†’build firewall (pure, offline,\n   deterministic reference fn + spec + unit tests) the proof depends on (FIX-8/18).\n   - *Research framing:* best-in-class mathematical exposition + algorithm comprehension â€” derivation-checking,\n     worked-example pedagogy, the Feynman technique, proof verification, dimensional/sanity analysis; how to\n     turn a paper's method prose into a verified, runnable reference. Persona tier = Fable 5 / Opus.\n3. **Literature review** (augmented researchPrime). Upstream lineage/lit-review is load-bearing for paper-repro.\n   - *Research framing:* systematic-review method, citation-lineage mining, recovering tacit knowledge from\n     cited code; what a rigorous lit/lineage report contains. Persona tier = Opus.\n4. **Data analysis** â€” find/clean/analyze/report.\n   - *Research framing:* best-in-class EDA, data cleaning/validation, result-comparison + plotting practice;\n     reproducible data pipelines. Persona tier = Sonnetâ†’Opus.\n5. **Analytic + ML code** â€” R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch.\n   - *Research framing:* best-in-class scientific/ML coding practice; satisfying a frozen firewall spec;\n     dependency-aware modular generation. Persona tier = Opus.\n6. **Code verification** (co-designed with #5).\n   - *Research framing:* best-in-class code-fidelity verification â€” visual artifacts a human can review,\n     chunked walkthroughs, executed-number checks bound to a verified module (FIX-8). Persona = Fable 5.\n\n### Stage C â€” recreate-a-paper proof cycle  [needs Stage B skills]\nIts own researchPrime (paper-repro pipeline SOTA â€” already partly done in Phase-0 research) + Crucible +\nForeman. Composes the Stage-B skills; required upstream lineage/lit-review; Assumptions Ledger; understandâ†’build\nfirewall; executed numbers BOUND to Ramanujan's pure reference fn; context-isolated advisory grader. The PROOF:\nreproduce Gelman ANOVA, graded on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (NOT fidelity).\n\n### Stage D â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration\nInject a known defect (a seeded deterministic-canary regression) into a built skill; a real sleep cycle must\nRECOVER it (regression-then-recovery) â€” a no-op cannot pass. The self-improving proof.\n\n### Later portfolio (own cycles, beyond this program's proof)\nJumper (brainstorm), doc-writing, legal analysis, propose-extensions recipe, then the productivity/personal\nstateful agents (model-agnostic; GWL/t2rs swap-in deferred â€” parallel track).\n\n## What stays fixed across all cycles (the substrate contract)\nPhase-0 infra (Stage A) + the Master Plan design pillars + the per-skill done-floor + PRINCIPLE-D (deterministic\ngate; advisory judging isolated) + the machine-checkable handoff contract. Each skill cycle inherits these; the\nresearch + Crucible add the per-skill METHOD on top.\n\n## Open question to revisit (separate from this sequence)\nAudit whether the TRIO skill PROTOCOLS (researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman SKILL.md method, not the engines)\nare themselves best-in-class â€” a small researchPrime \"is this protocol SOTA for its domain?\" pass over each.\nThe engines are demonstrably robust (the adversarial loops caught real flaws this program, including a wrong\nfix); the method-depth of the protocols is the open question.\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
