{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AAepzfvkZHVba4Ycj9tadw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## portfolio-program â€” planning trio session summary\n\n**What this session is**\n- A Crucible planning trio session (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) that produced a frozen design + Foreman-ready Phase-0 implementation plan for the Skill Foundry \"portfolio program.\" No build has run yet â€” `EXECUTION-LOG.md` records \"_no waves executed yet â€” awaiting Foreman invocation_.\"\n- Provenance chain: ENGINE-verified Phase-0 researchPrime run â†’ Crucible Stage 0 lock â†’ Stage 1 Master Plan (now **v4**, reached after **3 Shark-Tank rounds to convergence**) â†’ Stage 2 â†’ Foreman handoff (`DESCRIPTION.md`, `CRUCIBLE-INTAKE.md`).\n\n**Locked North Star (program-level)**\n- Build a deep, **self-improving, model-agnostic** skill repository where every skill carries a LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved in \"sleep\" sessions **without drifting**.\n- First end-to-end proof: a `recreate-a-paper` recipe reproducing the **Gelman ANOVA paper**, graded on **architecture/handoff success â€” NOT reproduction fidelity** (locked as Option A; extend-own-work is a deferred second slice).\n\n**Two-document structure of the session**\n- `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` covers **Phase 0 only** â€” the shared substrate (6 contiguous, TAP-gated waves). It is the immediate Foreman handoff.\n- `crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md` is the \"uber plan\": the full effort is a substrate build (Stage A) followed by **per-skill cycles**, each its OWN researchPrime â†’ skill-Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle â€” explicitly NOT one monolithic build (corrected by FIX-12 on 2026-06-20).\n\n**Phase-0 waves (the planned substrate)**\n- Wave 1: eval-harness go/no-go spike + test-harness bootstrap (proves wrapped validators emit real TAP the Foreman gate counts; prose-coverage path passes the vacuous-green guard; an unreachable advisory host leaves the gate GREEN).\n- Wave 2: one harness, three pluggable TAP-emitting validators â€” schema/path-existence, deterministic canary eval, numeric-tolerance grader.\n- Wave 3: machine-checkable handoff-contract gate (schema-valid + artifact_refs resolve + north_star round-trips byte-identical + open_questions empty).\n- Wave 4: per-skill repo templates + net-new logical-tierâ†’model table + a **swap test** (swap table â†’ resolved model changes, zero SKILL.md edits; pinned to the gemini-cli driver so it doesn't pass vacuously).\n- **Wave 5 (the anchor)**: 7-field journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill â†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback), TAP-tested on **fixture** journals (real skills don't exist yet). Done-when asserts three behaviors: a lesson advancing a machine-checkable non-goal is **rejected** (NS3 anti-drift); a candidate regressing a frozen canary is **blocked + rolled back** (NS2); a lesson corroborated only by same-context repetition is **not shipped** (R5 cross-context requirement).\n- Wave 6: Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning (append-only; deletion = human call) + citation hygiene (SkillsBenchâ†’arXiv 2602.12670, MemoryGraft dropped).\n\n**Key governing design decisions (Shark-Tank-hardened)**\n- **PRINCIPLE-D**: the no-regression gate emits TAP verdicts from **deterministic checks only**; all LLM / cross-family judging is **advisory and isolated** (FIX-15), so an unreachable advisory host can never HALT the terminal Foreman gate. This corrected a *wrong* v2 fix (FIX-7) caught in round 2.\n- Deterministic guarantees rest on the two artifacts the **orchestrator owns** (the TAP gate result it runs itself + a post-execute test-file content-hash baseline), since Foreman discards sub-agent transcripts â€” the plan does NOT try to prove \"an LLM genuinely ran.\"\n- Persona = method + **logical tier**; the tierâ†’model co